; The built-in `Int` extern must be emitted when the ONLY references to it come from emitted type
; aliases. `generate_int` is gated on `is_referenced("Int")`, whose reference walk covers emitted
; type aliases (not just rust structs), so a rule that classifies as a plain `pub type` alias over an
; `int`-bearing base still registers the reference and gets its `Int` definition. Regression: the walk
; visited rust structs only, so an alias-only `int` reference emitted `pub type X = Int;` naming an
; `Int` no one minted (`cannot find type Int`, E0425) — a dangle in both the rust and wasm crates.
;
; The two rules here span the first two legs of the descent the fix must cover: `bare_int` is a
; top-level `Rust(Int)` alias base; `cbor_int` nests it under a `.cbor` bytes wrapper (a wrapper
; STRUCT since the `.cbor` rule-body force-wrap, whose inner is the `Int`-bearing base the walk
; must still descend through). The table-VALUE leg (`Map(_, Rust(Int))` under `.cbor`) lives in
; cbor_int_table.cddl — split out because its inline-map controller
; (`bytes .cbor { * tstr => int }`) is a PARSE error for the ruby `cddl` gem (0.12.14; the gap in
; draft/ruby-cddl-inline-composite-control-arg-gap.md), and a spec-parse failure poisons every
; rule in its fixture for the `ir_conformance_corpus` ruby sweep. Kept apart, `bare_int` and
; `cbor_int` stay ruby-judgeable. Both rules are UNCONSTRAINED — a control (e.g. `int .ne 1`)
; instead makes a RangeCheck wrapper STRUCT that the rust-struct walk already covered, so the
; alias classification is exactly the untested path. The control sibling lives in
; tagged_constrained_int.cddl (`cbor_ctl_ne = bytes .cbor (int .ne 1)`, with a holder).
;
; Deliberately holder-FREE: embedding either of these in a record member (`h = [f: bare_int]`)
; registers `Int` through the record's field walk, and `Int` is a crate-global extern emitted once
; for the whole crate — so a single holder would define `Int` for the whole fixture and MASK the
; alias-only dangle this fixture exists to pin (the same batch-masking that let the class hide
; behind int-referencing batch-mates in the recombination sweep). The round-trip/decode side is
; covered by the decode-conformance CORPUS leg, which holder-wraps each rule in its own synthetic
; probe (`__probe_holder = [0, <rule>]`).
bare_int = int
cbor_int = bytes .cbor int
